<p>There is no row in which both premises are true (indeed, these are contradictory premises; the second is the negation of the first).  Thus for every row in which both premises are true (i.e., no row), the conclusion is also true.  Therefore the deduction rule is valid.  (This is an example of how everything follows from a contradiction.)</p>
</solution>
